    "type": "Discussion",
    "prompt": "You should spend about 40 minutes on this task. i i i Important research has already been done for decades on the negative effects i i of gaming, including addiction, depression and aggression. However, many i people believe that playing video games may boost children's learning, problem-solving skills and social skills. Write an essay to an educated reader to discuss both views and give your opinion. Include reasons and any relevant examples to support your answer. You should write at least 250 words. Your response will be evaluated",
    "B1": "Nowadays many people, especially children are keen on playing video games.\nWhile I accept that it is good for their learning and developing many skills, I believe\nthat it brings them negative effects.\nOn the one hand, there are several advantages of playing video games. First of\nall, it helps children reduce stress after hard study at school. When players play some\ninteresting games and enter the online world, they can feel relaxed and excited.\nSecondly, it improves children's imagination and creativity. While playing games,\nthey have to try to solve problems, think logically and become creative to get the\nhighest point or win the games. Learning these skills is also useful for their study and\nreal life. Finally, children can develop social skills. For example, thousands of people\n30 de thi viet lugn Tieng Anh B1, B2 VSTEP 149\n\n^Mim\nin the world join the virtual world of a game, so children have chances to make new\nfriends with other gamers and improve social relationships.\nOn the other hand, playing games has many disadvantages. The first drawback\nis that it is bad for children's health. Because children easily get game addiction,\nthey may spend most time playing games instead of going out and doing exercise.\nTherefore, they may get a lot of diseases such as overweight or back pain and feel tired.\nMoreover, playing games distracts children from their study. Kids tend to waste a lot\nof time playing games, so they do not focus on study and may get bad marks. Lastly,\nit affects their behaviors badly. There are violent actions in most games; therefore,\nchildren might copy these bad things and behaviors in their real life.\nIn conclusion, playing computer games is both positive and negative. It seems to\nme that the dangers of video games are more than their benefits. Parents should limit\nchildren's time of playing games to make them focus on their study and real life.",
    "B2": "In modern life, video gomes hove attracted the interest of many people, especially\nchiIdren. While I accept that video games have positive impacts on children, I also\nbelieve that kids' lives might be ruined by playing these games.\nOn the one hand, playing video games offers kids great advantages. The most\nobvious one is that most games are created for entertainment purposes. Entering\nimaginary worlds of some interesting games gives children the feeling of excitement\nand promotes relaxation. In the second place, computer games stimulate children's\nimagination and creativity. Playing games such as a puzzle requires children to have\nproblem-solving skills and logical thinking so as to get the highest point or win the\ngames, which is advantageous for their study and real life. Last but not least, gaming\nenables children to enhance social skills. For example, multiplayer games become\nvirtual social worlds for thousands of players worldwide; consequently, taking part in\nthese games allows children to have a larger circle of friends and broaden their social\nrelationships.\nOn the other hand, there are some of playing computer\ngames. First and foremost, it leaves harmful effects on children's health. It is easy for\nchildren to get addicted to games; as a result, spending lots of time getting stuck in\nfront of computer screens may lead them to suffer from a lot of physical and mental\nhealth problems such as obesity, eye strain, exhaustion and so on. Moreover, video\ngames make children distracted from their study. As a result, they may get bad learning\nresults. The final negative side is that gaming impacts children's emotional and social\nbehaviors severely. Many games contain violent actions or aggressive characters;\ntherefore, children possibly imitate problem behaviors in their daily life.\n30 de thi viet lugn Tieng Anh B1, B2 VSTEP 151\n\nMat khde, viec choi trd choi tren may tinh cd mot so hdu qua tieu cue. Thu nhdt,\n^ivmn\nnd cd nhung tdc hgi ddi vdi sue khde cua tre em. Tre em dd bi nghien game; do do,\nviec danh nhieu thoi gian ngbi trudc man hinh may tinh cd the khien chung gap phdi\nInnh iseuum vmana rdye, vite issu ue nkdhednei athbele c hthaat tv dv itdineho thgaanm nesh uhbaevoe pbhoi,t hm boei nmeafti,c imale ta mndo i,n ve.vg.a Htivoen\nsidensu;a h, otrwde cvhero, i tdhieeinr ctoun ksh fieanr otruet wbei ipghhd tnh etdirm p rtorosn. gT hhegrce ftoarpe., Kit eist qaudav isIda bclheu tnhga tc dp atrheen tbsi\nconkterot lq tuhae ihr gcch tiladpr ekne'rsn .t iMmae to tife pul acuyein cgu dgia cmunegs dsoo ltah acth cohi igldarmene cdannh hfoucdunsg o nng thhieemir strtgudnyg\nandd erne ahl dlnifeh. vi xd hgi vd cam xue cua tre em. Nhieu fro choi cd cdc hdnh dong bgo luc\nhogc cdc nhdn vat hung han; do do, tre co the bat chudc cdc hdnh vi cd van de trong"
